      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Density in seawater is primarily governed by temperature and salinity; cooler waters are denser, and saltier waters are denser at a given temperature. In deep-sea environments, a rapid temperature drop increases water density significantly. This sharp density increase, especially in stratified layers, can enhance the stability of a halocline by increasing the density gradient resisting vertical mixing.",
