    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The conductivity sensor seems to be the main issue—the data is just completely chaotic in that specific depth range. I'm worried there might be a hardware glitch or something affecting the signal integrity. Are there any specific common causes for these kinds of sudden, unpredictable data jumps in deep-sea deployments?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
